  "result": "Excellent! All 161 tests pass. I've successfully implemented payment tracking for invoices:\n\n**Created `src/payments.js` with:**\n\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` function that:\n  - Validates invoice is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (NOT_ISSUED error otherwise)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Checks payment doesn't exceed balance due (OVERPAYMENT error)\n  - Adds payment to invoice.payments array (creates array if missing)\n  - Updates status:\n    - 'partially_paid' when 0 < payments < total\n    - 'paid' when payments >= total\n  - Never mutates input invoice\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) with updated state\n\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` function that:\n  - Calculates invoice total minus sum of all payments\n  - Returns 0 if already paid or no payments yet\n  - Handles missing payments array\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added NOT_ISSUED error\n- Added OVERPAYMENT error\n- AMOUNT_INVALID already existed\n\n**Tests added (14 new payment tests):**\n- Recording payments on issued invoices\n- NOT_ISSUED validation for draft/paid invoices\n- AMOUNT_INVALID for non-positive or non-integer amounts\n- OVERPAYMENT detection\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Multiple payment accumulation\n- Non-mutation guarantees\n- balanceDue calculations for various payment states\n- Edge cases (VAT-exempt items, already-paid invoices)\n\nAll 161 tests pass. The payment system integrates seamlessly with the invoice totals calculation, handling discounts and VAT properly.",
